@startuml codex-renewal
!theme plain
title Slice 1, qualification/adoption pending: Codex personal plan: one auth owner refreshes; launches use external tokens and renew within a deadline

participant "Codex app-server\n(agent OS account, no auth.json)" as A
participant "Live agent-side executor / later session runner\nagent OS account; lease holder and app-server client" as E
participant "swarma-credential-broker: internal auth owner\nbroker service UID; broker-owned home + lock" as O
participant "Existing service manager\nqualified containment / kill-and-confirm" as M
participant "Approved Codex executable\nbroker UID; vendor refresh writer" as V
database "Broker-owned attempt evidence\nand durable vendor home" as S

E -> O: lease.request {harness: codex_cli, channel: external-token, …}
O -> O: verify lease checks 1–7 (active UID/generation and binding,\nlease + caller chains, current revocations, source/network qualification, R-TIME max/min checks)
break restore fenced or prior writer / store / outcome unresolved
  O --> E: revocation_state_unavailable / lease_owner_unavailable; no material
end
O -> O: trusted-time watermarked token expiry within 48 h? refresh once under the lifecycle gate
opt refresh required and safe
  O -> S: persist account-scoped attempt intent before launch
  O -> M: launch approved executable in qualified containment
  M -> V: one writer for the account
  V -> S: vendor rotates and persists native login
  M --> O: qualified writer-lifecycle evidence
  O -> S: reload durable home; resolve/persist attempt outcome
end
O -> O: repeat current authorization, R-TIME and restore fence under state lock before release
O --> E: payload {access_token, chatgpt_account_id, plan_type?}
E -> A: start private app-server; executor remains its client (§9.3)
E -> A: initialize (experimental capability required for external tokens)
E -> A: account/login/start {type: chatgptAuthTokens, accessToken, chatgptAccountId}
... turns ...
A -> A: model call answers 401
A -> E: account/chatgptAuthTokens/refresh (answer expected within ~10 s)
E -> O: lease.renew {lease_id, rejected_sha256} (deadline 8 s)
O -> O: check lease ownership and repeat checks 1–7 including restore fence
break previous writer / store / outcome unresolved
  O --> E: lease_owner_unavailable; no replacement refresh
  E --> A: error answer; turn fails
end
alt rejected token is still current
  O -> O: prior writer/outcome resolved; durable intent before contained refresh;\nresolve attempt and reload durable home (N rejected launches -> 1 writer)
end
alt renewed within the deadline and authorisation still valid
  O -> O: after refresh, repeat authorisation, R-TIME and restore fence under state lock\nimmediately before releasing material
  O --> E: payload {access_token, chatgpt_account_id}
  E -> E: verify same chatgpt_account_id as the lease
  alt account ID matches
    E --> A: refresh answer {accessToken, chatgptAccountId}
    A -> A: retry the call
  else account ID differs
    E -> E: verification fails; do not forward token\nerror/recovery unspecified in spec §9.3
  end
else timeout or refusal
  O --> E: renew_timeout | lease_reauth_required | …
  E --> A: error answer (no late reply, no fallback login)
  A -> A: the turn fails
end
opt live holder releases its lease when ending execution (§8.5)
  E -> O: lease.release {lease_id} (idempotent; ends renewal)
end
note over E,O
  No exec replacement of this client; renewal needs it alive (§9.3).
  Teardown/release ordering and init-failure / runner-loss cleanup:
  unspecified in spec §18.7; this opt is a permitted release, not a new policy.
  Without release: authorized_until bounds renewal; revocation stops
  new leases/renewals; unbind ends leases (§6.4, §7.2, §8.5).
  Release cannot erase a copied access token (§12.1).
end note
note over O: the refresh token never leaves the broker's store;\nlease_grant_revoked / lease_caller_revoked refuse renewal
note over E,A: one private app-server per execution; ephemeral storage pinned,\nno broker-mode codex exec and no shared-file/copy fallback
note over O
  Broker persists account/secret, grants/revocations, binding and lease metadata;
  helper owns UID/generation ledger. Refresh uses the approved vendor executable
  under broker UID; stable lock covers read / refresh / reload (§9.4).
  Lock alone cannot cover daemon death: at most one live vendor writer
  across replacement; durable attempt intent before contained launch.
  [[../spec/broker.md#93-external-token-mode Spec §9.3]]
  [[lease-recovery.puml M-CB2: timeout, transient failure, reauth and disconnect]]
end note
note over E,O
  Rejected token -> reauth_required, owner re-enrols; stopped owner ->
  owner_unavailable; safe transient failure -> backoff only after prior
  writer/outcome resolved and token valid (§9.4). Timeout may be ambiguous.
  Transient-to-active and owner-restart transitions unspecified in spec §9.4.
  Failed external-token initialisation -> external_token_init_failed (§9.3).
end note
== Independent daemon-replacement recovery case (§9.4, §15) ==
O -> O: daemon dies during refresh; replacement refresh stays closed
M -> V: contain and kill previous writer and all writer descendants
alt complete qualified process absence confirmed
  M --> O: previous writer absent
  O -> S: recover same attempt; reload durable vendor home
  alt prior outcome and store conclusively resolved; retry safe
    O -> O: allow account owner recovery; any next refresh uses new durable intent
  else external rotation / store / outcome ambiguous
    O -> O: owner_unavailable or reauth_required; no blind retry
    note over O,S
      Child death does not prove rotation failed. Re-enrolment
      requires confirmed writer absence; no login fallback.
    end note
  end
else surviving writer, interrupted cleanup or unavailable process evidence
  M --> O: lifecycle unresolved
  O -> O: owner_unavailable; no replacement refresh or re-enrolment writer
end
note over O,M
  Slice 1 activation requires platform-qualified containment and every
  daemon-death / rotation / replacement row in §9.6 on macOS and Linux.
  Concrete unit settings and attempt/process record formats unpublished (§18.10).
end note
note over O,V
  R-SVC-EGRESS v1: broker/vendor network only through its dedicated proxy.
  Explicit proxy variables for network-using children; no direct fallback.
  Qualified login/refresh/policy-fetch and resolver isolation gate v1 (§15.2).
  Safe proxy failure -> refresh_failed_transient/backoff only after
  writer/outcome resolution; ambiguous rotation stays unavailable (§9.4).
  R-FATE: user manager §7 fate table owns stop/crash/replacement rows.
  R-LOCK: state lock released for platform calls; retain account writer ownership;
  per-record in-flight marker and late-result revalidation (§13.1).
end note
note over E,O
  R-TIME: authorized_until and expiry at max(now, watermark),
  not_before at min(now, watermark); untrusted time refuses renewal.
  R-REBIND ends old leases; new binding cannot renew this lease.
  Fenced fresh-lease handoff is OPEN (§18.11); explicit park/restart until then.
end note
@enduml
